This procedure is equivalent to interpolation with Taylor's formula 3.6.4.

**Example 18**.: In the plane triangle \(ABC\), \(a{=}123\), \(B{=}29^{\circ}16^{\prime}\), \(c{=}321\); find \(A\), \(b\).

\[b^{2}{=}a^{2}{+}c^{2}{-}2ac\cos B{=}(123)^{2}{+}(321)^{2}\] \[-2(123)(321)\cos 29^{2}16^{\prime}\] \[b{=}221.99934\ 00\] \[\sin A{=}\frac{a\sin\,B}{b}{=}\frac{(123)(4.48887\ 50196)}{221.99934\ 00}{=}27086\ 39918\] \[A{=}15^{9}42^{\prime}56.469^{\prime\prime}.\]

